head downstairs for breakfast. The bags on my tired eyes revealed that I hadn’t had much sleep the previous night, but I was too tired and too hungry to hide them with makeup. When I reached the ground floor, I heard flusters and I became aware that Sebastian hadn’t gone to work yet. Suddenly, for some reason, I wished I had made myself somewhat more presentable.
